Subject: C interface: a draw's binding tables are the command buffer's, and argument buffers are asked of a program once

drawCommon made two Bindings for every draw -- six vectors taken from the heap and given back -- and called
bindArgumentBuffers for both stages, which copies the stage's buffer table before it looks whether any resource is
an argument buffer's member at all (3.4% of the render thread on the phone, a third of it in malloc: perfil-1).

- The two tables are hakios_metal_cb's own (vsBindings, fsBindings), emptied and filled again: what they take from
  the heap is taken once a command buffer. One draw at a time records into a command buffer, deferred or not.
- CompiledProgram::argumentBuffers says whether either stage has such a member, found out at the program's first
  draw. With none, bindArgumentBuffers changed nothing; it is not called.

The words recorded are the same (golden streams). drawbench, A610 constants, the C interface with the phone's
stages, heap allocations a draw: S 6.2 -> 1.2, T 5.8 -> 0.8.


